      "id": 1,
      "text": "Shelburne was first settled in 1756 as part of Deerfield, then called Deerfield Northwest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofshelburnema.gov/p/27/History"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1775 Shelburne was incorporated, named after William Petty, the 2nd Earl of Shelburne.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofshelburnema.gov/p/27/History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Glacial Potholes in Shelburne Falls are a waterfall with dozens of rock‑drilled potholes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shelburne%2C_Massachusetts"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Troy & Greenfield Railroad arrived in 1867, followed by the Shelburne Falls and Colrain Street Railway in 1896.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
